{"season":2026,"week":12,"kind":"preview","league":"67FFL","my_team":"ATX Bowers","generated_utc":"2026-11-26T22:58Z","writer":"claude","headline":"Week 12 preview: Watson is the one real upgrade on waivers","dek":"Your lineup projects to 121.8, sixth in the league, and quarterback is the biggest gap to close.","sections":[{"id":"my_lineup","title":"Your best lineup","md":"Our projection has ATX Bowers at **121.8** points, sixth of 12 in the league. Just Win Baby leads at 150.8.\n\n- **QB:** Geno Smith (12.4)\n- **RB:** Tony Pollard (16.46), Quinshon Judkins (11.06)\n- **WR:** DeVonta Smith (16.67), Chris Olave (15.27)\n- **TE:** George Kittle (12.85)\n- **FLEX:** Deebo Samuel Sr. (10.63), Denzel Boston (10.46)\n- **K:** Tyler Bass (8.05)\n- **DEF:** TB D/ST (7.99)\n\nYour Week 12 waiver claims went through: Smith, Bass and TB D/ST are on your roster, and NYJ D/ST is back in the free-agent pool.\n\nCompared with the league median at each position:\n- **QB:** 12.4 vs 18.1, well below.\n- **RB:** 27.5 vs 38.4, well below.\n- **WR:** 53.0 vs 33.5, your strength by a wide margin.\n- **TE:** 12.8 vs 11.3, slightly above.\n\nTwo injury tags to watch:\n- **Denzel Boston** did not practice (quadricep). He's in your lineup at FLEX, so check his status before kickoff.\n- **DeVonta Smith** was a full practice participant with a hamstring tag, so he's fine to start.\n\nNobody on your roster is on a bye or listed unavailable."},{"id":"close_calls","title":"Close calls","md":"**FLEX: Denzel Boston (10.46) over Brenton Strange (10.33), margin 0.13**\n- Our projection is nearly even, but the usage points to Boston. He has a 90% season snap share, **11.5** xFP over his last 3 and a 19% target share.\n- Strange sits at 5.0 xFP and an 8% target share over his last 3. His appeal is JAX's **32.0** implied points against TEN, which is a big team total.\n- The catch is the Boston DNP. If he's out, Strange or Omarion Hampton (10.06) steps in, so check his status before you lock the lineup.\n\n**FLEX: Deebo Samuel Sr. (10.63) over Omarion Hampton (10.06), margin 0.57**\n- Our projection leans Deebo, but his recent usage doesn't back it up. His snap share is 54% over his last 3, and his xFP is only **6.4** against 12.0 actual points per game.\n- Hampton's usage is the stronger of the two at 10.6 xFP and a 53% snap share. His team is the problem, since LAC's implied total is just 16.5 against NE.\n- Deebo's scoring has run well ahead of his usage. SF's implied total of 23.2 against SEA is what keeps him in. This is close to a coin flip, and I'd lean Deebo only because of the better game environment."},{"id":"waivers","title":"Waiver adds and streamers","md":"**QB: the one clear upgrade**\n- **Deshaun Watson** (CLE, 17.99) projects **5.6** points above Geno Smith (12.4) in our model. He's also the highest-projected QB on the waiver list.\n- His usage is steady: 99% snaps and 14.5 xFP over his last 3, with CLE implied at 22.5 against LV.\n- He shares a game with Judkins and Boston, so your Browns exposure gets concentrated. That's fine as a stack, but it's one game script.\n- The other options all project above Smith too: Joe Milton III (15.51, only 2 games of data), Bryce Young (14.3) and Jacoby Brissett (14.05).\n- You'd need to drop a bench player to add one.\n\n**K and DEF**\n- **Drew Stevens** (WAS, 9.02) projects about 1 point above Bass (8.05).\n- The dropped **NYJ D/ST** (9.15) now projects higher than TB D/ST (7.99). It faces MIA, implied at 17.5. NYG D/ST (9.11) is the other option. TB D/ST is a fine hold, but the gap favors NYJ.\n\n**RB and TE: nothing that beats your starters**\n- RB: Rachaad White (8.54) and Austin Ekeler (8.38) sit below your FLEX options. Ekeler's snaps are up to 41% over his last 3.\n- TE: Cade Otton (9.64) is the best of the group, and Kittle is well clear of him.\n\n**WR: depth only**\n- Max Hurleman (PIT, 10.87) is a one-game sample, and PIT's implied total is 16.0. I wouldn't chase it.\n- Xavier Hutchinson (HOU, 10.13) has snaps up from 61% to 80%, a 17% target share and a 27.0 implied total.\n- Darius Cooper (PHI) has a 22% target share and 94% snaps over his last 3.\n- Adonai Mitchell (NYJ) has 12.1 xFP over his last 3 against 4.6 actual points, so his scoring has lagged his usage.\n- None of them clears your current FLEX projections."},{"id":"buy_sell","title":"Buy low, sell high","md":""},{"id":"around_league","title":"Around the league: needs and trade fits","md":"The deadline passed in Week 11, and no trade fits were flagged for ATX Bowers anyway. This is a read on who's thin, not a list of deals.\n\n- **Just Win Baby (9-2):** best projection in the league at 150.8, driven by a **70.1** WR group. RB is the need, at 31.0 against a 38.4 median.\n- **Chentudo El Venudo (8-3):** projects only 112.1 and needs QB, RB and TE. Kenneth Walker III is listed Out with a groin injury. This is the most vulnerable record in the top group.\n- **Moore Than A Bite (8-3):** needs WR and TE. Josh Jacobs is Questionable with a finger injury.\n- **SMA (7-4):** Dalton Kincaid is Questionable with a thumb injury.\n- **Lover Boys (3-8)** and **Bucky Charms (3-8):** both need a QB and are the thinnest at the position.\n- **Your own team (1-10):** needs QB and RB. Your WR group is strong at 53.0, second only to Just Win Baby and level with Chentudo El Venudo (53.2)."}],"links":{"Geno Smith":"p:00-0030565","Tony Pollard":"p:00-0035261","Quinshon Judkins":"p:00-0040784","DeVonta Smith":"p:00-0036912","Chris Olave":"p:00-0037239","George Kittle":"p:00-0033288","Tyler Bass":"p:00-0036162","TB D/ST":"d:TB","Deebo Samuel Sr.":"p:00-0035719","Denzel Boston":"p:00-0041037","Brenton Strange":"p:00-0038935","Omarion Hampton":"p:00-0040666","Deshaun Watson":"p:00-0033537","Joe Milton III":"p:00-0039398","Bryce Young":"p:00-0039150","Jacoby Brissett":"p:00-0033119","Rachaad White":"p:00-0037256","Austin Ekeler":"p:00-0033699","Audric Estime":"p:00-0039373","Devin Singletary":"p:00-0035250","Max Hurleman":"p:00-0